      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FIRE AND PASSION (7) is flying having won four straight, including a six-metre victory at Albion Park over 2138m in a 1:54.8 mile rate against Move It Lou. He boasts a stellar track-and-distance record and is well-handled by Grant Dixon. However, his move from gate 1 to gate 7 provides MOVE IT LOU NZ (4) a way back into contention. After two second-place finishes, including a close second in NR up to 75 company, he also receives a class drop. Although he was clearly behind FIRE AND PASSION last start, he is building in fitness and the draw change makes him a chance to turn the tables. HAVTIMETODREAM NZ (3) was a beaten odds-on favourite when resuming last time in NR up to 75 grade but will be fitter and has three wins from four Albion Park starts, keeping her in the mix. FUGITIVE NZ (6) resumed with a strong fourth, finishing just under three metres behind, and his distance record suggests good each-way value if he progresses second-up.",
